SUMMARY:Migrating Monarchs
DESCRIPTION:All programs at Prairie Ridge currently require registration.  Register\nJoin us for a front-row seat to one of nature’s most incredible journeys\, the Monarch butterfly migration! We’ll start this family friendly program in our Nature Neighborhood Garden to explore the habitats we steward here at Prairie Ridge and see how these spaces fuel Monarchs along their trek south. Then\, we’ll head into the prairie to spot as many butterflies as we can! If we’re lucky\, we might even catch and release a live Monarch butterfly. We will learn about the Monarch Larvae Monitoring Project and Monarch Watch collaborative science projects along the way.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/migrating-monarchs/
LOCATION:Prairie Ridge\, 1671 Gold Star Drive\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27607\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,Children,Collaborative Science,Educators,K-12 Students,Outdoor Experiences,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Julie%20Hall":MAILTO:julie.hall@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.812182885871;-78.713963528554
